cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using these metadata."
title: "LBM_isca: a Linear Baroclinic Model on the Isca/GFDL spectral core"
abstract: >-
  LBM_isca is a moist, dynamics-only Linear Baroclinic Model whose dynamical
  core is a linearisation of the Isca / GFDL atmos_spectral primitive
  equations (Simmons-Burridge vertical differencing, pure-sigma coordinate,
  semi-implicit leapfrog with a Robert-Asselin filter), at T42 L20 on a numpy
  (CPU) or CuPy (CUDA GPU) backend. Because it is re-derived from the GPLv3
  Isca sources rather than from the proprietary Watanabe-Kimoto ln_solver, it
  can be distributed freely under the GPL.
type: software
authors:
  - name: "kuiper2000"
version: "0.1.0"
license: GPL-3.0-or-later
repository-code: "https://github.com/kuiper2000/LBM_isca"
keywords:
  - linear baroclinic model
  - atmospheric dynamics
  - spectral primitive equations
  - teleconnections
  - Isca
  - GFDL
